        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4c0adcd4-2a5d-3f0e-bb0b-2f9042fcb6cd",
                "word": "doomscrolling",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ccf0af04-3762-3825-8380-0211b9a988f2",
                        "entry_id": "4c0adcd4-2a5d-3f0e-bb0b-2f9042fcb6cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Consommation compulsive d'informations sur Internet, en particulier relatant des catastrophes ou des faits divers d’actualité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd4548c-d45d-4b11-91c8-5cb5880f1d5b",
                                "sense_id": "ccf0af04-3762-3825-8380-0211b9a988f2",
                                "text": "Les gens souffrant de « doomscrolling » ne peuvent pas s’empêcher de regarder les dernières nouvelles, sur les réseaux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6609098-4932-49c6-a98b-2bdeef0dd387",
                                "sense_id": "ccf0af04-3762-3825-8380-0211b9a988f2",
                                "text": "Un “doomscrolling” excessif peut avoir un impact néfaste sur la santé physique et mentale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "053446d9-0d1d-4a48-9681-dcdc646692bb",
                                "sense_id": "ccf0af04-3762-3825-8380-0211b9a988f2",
                                "text": "Ceci dit, pour comprendre ce qui (nous) pousse à ce «défilement morbide» (appellation québécoise du doomscrolling), il faut apprendre les ressorts de l'économie de l'attention, saisir finement quels sont les processus qui nous traversent lorsqu'on est confronté aux stratégies mises en œuvre par les industries du numérique (dark pattern, design émotionnel, notamment)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f5ef136-e5e1-340c-bbaa-b26cbee75aa3",
                        "entry_id": "4c0adcd4-2a5d-3f0e-bb0b-2f9042fcb6cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sentiment d'anxiété résultant de cette pratique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56a4c4fb-4a50-4215-9694-0d80bc13856e",
                                "sense_id": "6f5ef136-e5e1-340c-bbaa-b26cbee75aa3",
                                "text": "Pour ne pas sombrer dans le doomscrolling, elle se déconnecte régulièrement de Twitter."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07422f7a-9206-469e-b88d-5bf34d74aa21",
                        "source_entry_id": "4c0adcd4-2a5d-3f0e-bb0b-2f9042fcb6cd",
                        "target_lang_word": "doomscrolling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "doomscrolling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                        "entry_id": "ac650ee6-1947-3cfc-aedc-44fb13ea46ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice of continually reading Internet news about catastrophic events."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "neologism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "494c3aea-424e-410e-b585-3001b6eb80a7",
                                                "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                                "text": "Step 1 is to acknowledge the burden that doomscrolling creates for our health, Dr. Gazzaley said. “You have to realize you don’t want to live your life in a hamster wheel of complete news consumption,” he said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d6df952-602e-45c3-bd3b-d0f6928b2b08",
                                                "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                                "text": "I assured them that while doomscrolling was a difficult online pitfall, it wasn't one they needed to fall in to^([sic])."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "921d0deb-b83d-4415-aeff-6d97b5113d43",
                                                "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                                "text": "It would be easy enough to say just stop doing it, but with everything happening in the world right now, it’s impossible to completely avoid doomscrolling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35a8e879-9b3e-4d4d-9fe1-0a5e8a67f8f0",
                                                "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                                "text": "But this is 2021 and after a year and a half of COVID-19, of racial and socioeconomic unrest, viewers may be tuning in for a respite from doomscrolling daily news."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b68689b3-7109-4b7c-80ef-8494ec10780c",
                                                "sense_id": "e1d3d063-7c34-3b64-8539-24236e281549",
                                                "text": "Now doomscrolling is back in ways not seen since the beginning of the Covid pandemic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4df26c4-6488-31b1-b52b-630f6c050c08",
                                        "entry_id": "ac650ee6-1947-3cfc-aedc-44fb13ea46ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Continuously and aimlessly consuming any content on social media, particularly sites that utilize a scrolling format, such as Instagram, TikTok, and Twitter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
